MiPlaits: read the engine's functions from the constant interface table.

Since SuperSonic v0.95.0, one process can have more than one engine (World).
Each World has its own copy of the interface table, and PluginLoad gets that
copy as inTable. The copy goes away with its World. The old code kept inTable
in ft, so after the World that loaded the plugin last stops, ft points to
freed memory. ft now points to gInterfaceTable, the constant table that
SuperSonic's own plugins use. DefineDtorUnit still registers the UGen through
inTable, in the World that loads the plugin.

diff --git i/projects/MiPlaits/MiPlaits.cpp w/projects/MiPlaits/MiPlaits.cpp
index adc8944..7608348 100644
--- i/projects/MiPlaits/MiPlaits.cpp
+++ w/projects/MiPlaits/MiPlaits.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,10 @@ float kSampleRate = 48000.0f;
 float a0 = (440.0f / 8.0f) / kSampleRate;
 const size_t   kBlockSize = plaits::kBlockSize;
 
-static InterfaceTable *ft;
+// The engine's functions come from the one constant table. The table that
+// PluginLoad gets (inTable) belongs to one World and goes away with it, so
+// the plugin does not keep it.
+static const InterfaceTable* const ft = &gInterfaceTable;
 
 
 struct MiPlaits : public Unit {
@@ -239,7 +242,6 @@ void MiPlaits_next( MiPlaits *unit, int inNumSamples)
 
 
 PluginLoad(MiPlaits) {
-    ft = inTable;
     DefineDtorUnit(MiPlaits);
 }
 
